SUMMARY:SFJAZZ 2026-2027 Season
DESCRIPTION:The 26-27 SFJAZZ season\, entitled Forward Motion\, is led by Executive Artistic Director Terence Blanchard and CEO Gabrielle Armand. SFJAZZ notes\, “Across nine months and over 300 shows\, the music moves with purpose and possibility\, transforming our stages into a hub for innovation\, collaboration\, and discovery.” \nThey go on to note: “From centennial celebrations of Miles Davis\, John Coltrane\, Antonio Carlos Jobim\, and Ray Brown to performances by icons like Ron Carter\, Dianne Reeves\, and Branford Marsalis\, the season connects legacy to the now. Rising stars and modern masters alike—from Isaiah Collier\, Tyreek McDole\, Brandon Woody\, and Gabrielle Cavassa to Christian McBride\, Hiromi\, Julian Lage\, and Cécile McLorin Salvant—drive the music forward.” \nUpcoming concerts include Julian Lage Quartet (Oct 19)\, and Charles Tolliver for the John Coltrane celebration (Oct 25)\, and much more! \nSee the SFJAZZ site for more information and tickets. \n 
URL:https://sfciviccenter.org/event/sfjazz-2026-2027-season/
CATEGORIES:Music
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://sfciviccenter.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Screenshot-2026-09-28-at-1.45.02 PM.png
END:VEVENT
