SUMMARY:SF Symphony 2026-2027 Season
DESCRIPTION:The upcoming 2026-2027 season at the SF Symphony features a calendar full of debuts\, stars\, guest artists and much more. \nPremieres include a “work by Emerging Black Composers Project winner Kyle Rivera\, conducted by Juraj Valčuha\, and a new concerto for harp and percussion by Rene Orth\, conducted by Esa-Pekka Salonen and featuring Principal Percussion Jacob Nissly and Principal Harp Katherine Siochi.” \nSpecial concerts include “Jazz singer Samara Joy\, folk musician Gregory Alan Isakov\, and singer -songwriter Fantastic Negrito [as] each join the San Francisco Symphony for one-night -only performances [and] composer and conductor Joe Hisaishi [as he] leads the San Francisco Symphony in a program featuring his own music\, including a new SF Symphony-commissioned Concerto for Orchestra.” As well as\, “San Francisco Symphony celebrates Conductor Laureate Herbert Blomstedt’s 100th year with a January program featuring Schubert’s Symphony No. 3 and Bruckner’s Symphony No. 4\, Romantic.” \nThis is all in addition to their holiday performances\, special community events\, and Film with Live Orchestra series: Avatar\, Hook\, La La Land\, Metropolis\, Tim Burton’s The Nightmare Before Christmas\, The Ring\, Star Wars: Return of the Jedi\, and Up. \nSee their full calendar of performances and ticket purchasing information here.
URL:https://sfciviccenter.org/event/sf-symphony-2026-2027-season/
CATEGORIES:Community,Music,Theater
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://sfciviccenter.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Screen-Shot-2026-07-22-at-12.24.22-PM.png
END:VEVENT
