SUMMARY:San Francisco Opera 2026-2027 Season
DESCRIPTION:The San Francisco Opera’s 2026-2027 season opened with Opera Ball\, marking the Company’s 104th season. \nThe San Francisco Opera notes highlights include Thea Musgrave’s rarely performed 1977 opera\, Mary\, Queen of Scots\, (opening September 20th) starring soprano Heidi Stober\, as well as repertory revivals such as Mozart’s The Marriage of Figaro (opening October 31st) and Puccini’s Tosca (June 4th) with soprano Rachel Willis-Sørensen. Other wonderful operas include Manon (opening October 15th) and Das Rheingold (opening May 29th) and special events such as Strauss in Concert (November 6th) and the Rpide Conert (June 25th.) \nSee the SF Opera site for more information and tickets. \n 
URL:https://sfciviccenter.org/event/san-francisco-opera-2026-2027-season/
CATEGORIES:Music,Theater
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://sfciviccenter.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screen-Shot-2026-08-14-at-3.48.50-PM.png
