UID:13029-1794713400-1796450400@sfciviccenter.org
SUMMARY:Philharmonia Baroque Orchestra's Handel's The Power of Music & Baroque Brilliance
DESCRIPTION:This fall the Philharmonia Baroque Orchestra presents Handel’s The Power of Music & Baroque Brilliance at the Herbst Theatre: \nHandel’s The Power of Music \nMusic Director Peter Whelan leads the first U.S. performances of Handel’s 1742 Dublin version of Alexander’s Feast\, performed on period instruments and in the style of the time. The concerts feature soprano Sherezade Panthaki\, mezzo-soprano Rachael Wilson\, tenor James Way\, Philharmonia Baroque Orchestra\, and Philharmonia Chorale under the direction of Valérie Sainte-Agathe. \nProgram \nGeorge Frideric HANDEL — Alexander’s Feast\, or The Power of Music (1742 Dublin Version) (U.S. PREMIERE) \nPeter Whelan\, conductor\nSherezade Panthaki\, soprano\nRachael Wilson\, mezzo-soprano\nJames Way\, tenor\nPhilharmonia Chorale\, directed by Valérie Sainte-Agathe \nFriday\, November 13\, 2026 • 7:30 PM\nHerbst Theatre\, tickets here. \nBaroque Brilliance \nGuest conductor Patrick Dupré Quigley leads a festive holiday-season program featuring music by Handel\, J.S. Bach\, Telemann\, C.P.E. Bach\, and Marianna Martines with soprano Kathryn Mueller and Philharmonia principal cellist William Skeen. \nProgram \nHANDEL — “Let the Bright Seraphim”\nMarianna MARTINES — O virgo\, cui salutem debet orbis (WEST COAST PREMIERE)\nTELEMANN — Burlesque de Quixotte\nC.P.E. BACH — Cello Concerto in A major\nJ.S. BACH — Jauchzet Gott in allen Landen \nPatrick Dupré Quigley\, conductor\nKathryn Mueller\, soprano\nWilliam Skeen\, cello\nGonzalo X. Ruiz\, oboe\nKathryn Adduci\, trumpet \nFriday\, December 4\, 2026 • 7:30 PM\nHerbst Theatre\, tickets here.
URL:https://sfciviccenter.org/event/philharmonia-baroque-orchestras-handels-the-power-of-music-baroque-brilliance/
CATEGORIES:Music
