SUMMARY:SF Ballet 2026-2027 Season
DESCRIPTION:The 2026-2027 SF Ballet season begins with the beloved family holiday favorite Nutcracker (Dec 4-27)\, before the 94th Season Opening Night Gala in January. \nHighlights include Helgi Tomasson’s The Sleeping Beauty (Jan 29-Feb 7) a 19th century classic;  Titans of Choreography (Feb 16-21)\, which features diversity of three major contemporary European choreographers; George Balanchine’s Jewels (Feb 27-Mar 7)\, returning to the War Memorial Opera House in full for the first time since 2009; Balanchine’s A Midsummer Night’s Dream (Mar 19-27)\, with a journey through William Shakespeare’s enchanted forest; Divine Creatures (Apr 8-14)\, paying homage to Sergei Diaghilev’s revolutionary Ballets Russes with music by Andy Akiho; and the return of Sir Kenneth MacMillan’s Manon (Apr 23-May 2)\, considered one of the choreographer’s best. \nMore information and tickets on the SF Ballet site.
URL:https://sfciviccenter.org/event/sf-ballet-2026-2027-season/
